mode: build

--- OUT --->
7
7
--- IR --->
# an IR section reads main_build's dump in build mode, which is the *optimized release* IR - `echoc
# build` always runs the O3 pipeline, unlike `run`, which only optimizes when asked. so this is the one
# place in the corpus where that pipeline's effect on the reference counting runtime is asserted.
#
# and it removes all of it: the allocation, the retain for `$c = $b`, the two releases at scope end and
# the reads through the handle are all gone, and both echoes are folded to the constant 7. that is only
# sound because the counts balanced, so it is worth pinning
CHECK: i32 @main()
CHECK-NOT: call ptr @malloc
CHECK-NOT: call void @__eco_release
CHECK-NOT: strong.inc
CHECK: ret i32 0
